1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,550
A water-quality alert reveals a problem.

2
00:00:02,840 --> 00:00:06,850
Across a municipal network,
it rarely reveals where it began.

3
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:10,970
Sparse sensors can leave several
upstream sources plausible.

4
00:00:11,290 --> 00:00:13,180
Another sample costs time,

5
00:00:13,270 --> 00:00:17,710
while a reasonable-looking response can
reduce pressure or disrupt service elsewhere.

6
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:20,730
So the question is not only
what a model predicts.

7
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:24,430
It is what evidence is strong enough
to justify the next decision.

8
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:27,220
A proposed response must survive physics,

9
00:00:27,310 --> 00:00:29,220
then stop at a human boundary.

10
00:00:29,260 --> 00:00:31,390
HydroSwarm is offline,

11
00:00:31,430 --> 00:00:34,880
physics-first decision support
built around that distinction.

12
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:39,220
This checksummed Reference Incident
exposes the complete workflow.

13
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:41,230
From the first observation,

14
00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:45,770
HydroCore-v5 contributes learned evidence
to rank plausible sources,

15
00:00:45,860 --> 00:00:50,060
while uncertainty remains visible
instead of collapsing into one answer.

16
00:00:50,930 --> 00:00:52,710
When evidence is insufficient,

17
00:00:52,790 --> 00:00:55,830
HydroSwarm does not simply
ask the model again.

18
00:00:56,030 --> 00:00:59,940
A deterministic sampling policy identifies
a useful next measurement,

19
00:01:00,040 --> 00:01:02,350
and the workflow pauses for that evidence.

20
00:01:02,550 --> 00:01:04,730
Only then does the workflow advance.

21
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:08,360
When that sample arrives,

22
00:01:08,370 --> 00:01:10,390
the posterior changes sharply.

23
00:01:10,660 --> 00:01:12,710
The earlier prediction was evidence,

24
00:01:12,860 --> 00:01:14,580
not a permanent conclusion.

25
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:17,540
Next,

26
00:01:17,580 --> 00:01:20,260
response candidates are generated
deterministically

27
00:01:20,270 --> 00:01:24,330
and checked by exact WNTR
and EPANET simulation.

28
00:01:24,610 --> 00:01:26,520
The first candidate is rejected

29
00:01:26,540 --> 00:01:29,240
because it violates the configured
pressure constraint.

30
00:01:29,550 --> 00:01:32,030
A second satisfies
the modeled constraints

31
00:01:32,070 --> 00:01:33,550
and is marked verified.

32
00:01:33,740 --> 00:01:35,580
Proposal is not permission.

33
00:01:35,730 --> 00:01:38,680
Physics can veto
a plausible-looking response.

34
00:01:40,120 --> 00:01:43,180
And verified still does not mean executed.

35
00:01:43,750 --> 00:01:47,250
HydroSwarm has no
infrastructure-actuation authority.

36
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:51,150
The consequential step remains
a separate human approval boundary,

37
00:01:51,270 --> 00:01:55,390
with verification context and provenance
available for inspection.

38
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:59,960
The Technical Dock preserves
the network identity

39
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:02,800
and verification context
behind that decision.

40
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:07,540
That was the reproducible
Reference Incident.

41
00:02:07,870 --> 00:02:12,520
This is the frozen v0.2.1 runtime
on the same inputs.

42
00:02:12,810 --> 00:02:16,790
Here, no useful sample remains
while planning is unjustified.

43
00:02:17,130 --> 00:02:18,760
HydroSwarm stops.

44
00:02:19,060 --> 00:02:20,680
Rather than forcing a result.

45
00:02:20,720 --> 00:02:22,750
HydroCore-v5 is advisory.

46
00:02:22,790 --> 00:02:26,820
Calibration and deterministic OOD checks
bound its authority.

47
00:02:27,130 --> 00:02:29,500
Sampling and planning stay deterministic.

48
00:02:29,560 --> 00:02:32,560
WNTR and EPANET verify physics.

49
00:02:32,740 --> 00:02:34,540
Final approval stays human.

50
00:02:34,580 --> 00:02:37,000
The evaluation was locked before opening.

51
00:02:37,140 --> 00:02:40,050
Nominal Top-1 was 73.3%;

52
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:42,300
Top-3, 86.7%.

53
00:02:42,470 --> 00:02:45,120
Across 105 locked-final cases,

54
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:47,635
Top-1 was 55.2%,

55
00:02:47,675 --> 00:02:50,280
with 88.6% conformal coverage.

56
00:02:50,470 --> 00:02:51,835
On novel topology,

57
00:02:51,875 --> 00:02:53,710
localization signal remains,

58
00:02:53,730 --> 00:02:55,470
but calibration is inapplicable

59
00:02:55,510 --> 00:02:57,210
and actionable rate is zero.

60
00:02:57,420 --> 00:03:00,170
None of 15 hard safety counters
were violated.

61
00:03:00,260 --> 00:03:01,255
No rerun.

62
00:03:01,295 --> 00:03:02,670
No post-lock tuning.

63
00:03:02,710 --> 00:03:04,590
HydroSwarm runs locally

64
00:03:04,630 --> 00:03:07,460
and accepts standard EPANET
network models,

65
00:03:07,550 --> 00:03:10,640
keeping infrastructure data
in the operator environment.

66
00:03:10,680 --> 00:03:13,080
Every path ends in a governed decision.

67
00:03:13,260 --> 00:03:15,150
This is simulation-validated,

68
00:03:15,190 --> 00:03:16,730
not field-validated.

69
00:03:16,940 --> 00:03:19,080
The goal is not greater confidence.

70
00:03:19,310 --> 00:03:21,420
It is a more defensible decision.
